3 categories with 3 questions each (9 questions total), worth $100, $200, and $300
Each clue is shown as an answer, and the player must respond in the form of a question ("What is...?")
15-second time limit per clue
Score starts at $0. A correct response adds the clue's value, and a wrong or timed-out response subtracts it.
The game ends when all 9 clues are used, and then the final score is displayed
A flag variable, shouldRepeat, controls whether the player goes again

Logical steps

Start and set score = 0 and questionsLeft = 9
Display the board
Player picks a category and dollar value
Display the clue and start the timer
Get the player's response
Check whether the response is correct and phrased as a question
Yes: add the value to the score and show "Correct!"
No: subtract the value from the score and show the correct response
Mark the clue as used and subtract 1 from questionsLeft
If questionsLeft > 0, set shouldRepeat = "Yes". Otherwise set shouldRepeat = "No".
If shouldRepeat = "Yes", go back to step 2
Display the final score and end

Modules (to avoid repeated steps)

displayBoard(): shows the remaining clues
getSelection(): gets the category and value
askClue(): displays the clue, runs the timer, and gets the response
checkResponse(): tests whether the response is correct and in question form
updateScore(): adds or subtracts the clue's value
displayFinalScore(): shows the result at the end
